---
// Erawan privacy policy. Linked from the Erawan page footer and from the Google sign-in
// consent screen (Google Auth Platform → Branding → "Application privacy policy link").
// Every statement here describes what the program does; change it when the program changes.
import AppLayout from "../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro";

const home = "/apps/erawan/";
const updated = "13 November 2026";
---

<AppLayout
	title="Erawan privacy policy"
	description="What Erawan does with your files and your Google account: it runs on your computer, and nothing is sent to its authors."
>
	<div class="e-privacy">
		<p class="e-back"><a href={home}>← Erawan</a></p>
		<h1>Erawan privacy policy</h1>
		<p class="e-date">Last updated {updated}</p>

		<p>
			Erawan is a program you run on your own computer to back up files, consolidate folders and
			find duplicates. It has no server of its own and no account system. Its authors receive
			nothing from it: no files, no file names, no usage statistics and no crash reports.
		</p>

		<h2>What Erawan reads and where it goes</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Erawan reads the files and folders you select as a source, and their names, sizes, modification times and checksums.</li>
			<li>It copies them only to the destination you choose, such as a disk, a server you name, or your own cloud storage.</li>
			<li>Job settings, progress and logs are kept in a state directory on your computer. They include file names and paths.</li>
			<li>Erawan makes no network connections other than to the sources and destinations you configure. Transfers are carried out by <a href="https://rclone.org/" rel="noopener">rclone</a> and rsync, which run on your computer.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Google Drive</h2>
		<p>If you connect a Google Drive, you sign in to Google in your browser and Google asks you to approve the access.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>As a backup source</strong>, Erawan asks for read-only access. It lists and downloads the Drive files in the folder you choose, to copy them to your destination. It cannot change or delete anything in your Drive.</li>
			<li><strong>The sign-in token</strong> Google issues is stored in rclone's configuration file on your computer. It is not sent to Erawan's authors or to anyone else.</li>
			<li><strong>Your Google data</strong> is used only to carry out the backup you start. It is not shared, sold, used for advertising, or read by any person other than you.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Erawan's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
			<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
			including the Limited Use requirements.
		</p>

		<h2>Removing access and data</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Remove Erawan's access to your Google account at any time on Google's <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" rel="noopener">third-party connections page</a>.</li>
			<li>Delete the remote from rclone's configuration to remove the stored token.</li>
			<li>Delete Erawan's state directory to remove its job records. Your backed-up files stay wherever you copied them until you delete them.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>This website</h2>
		<p>This site is static pages. It sets no cookies and has no sign-in.</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:hello@indri.studio">hello@indri.studio</a>.</p>
	</div>
</AppLayout>

<style>
	.e-privacy {
		color: var(--color-on-surface);
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 28px 16px 64px;
	}
	.e-privacy a { color: var(--color-primary-container); }
	.e-privacy a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-primary-container); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 4px; }
	.e-privacy h1, .e-privacy h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
	.e-privacy h1 { font-size: 34px; margin: 12px 0 4px; }
	.e-privacy h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 32px 0 8px; }
	.e-privacy p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
	.e-privacy ul { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 22px; list-style: disc; }
	.e-privacy li { margin: 0 0 8px; }
	.e-back { margin: 0; }
	.e-back a { text-decoration: none; }
	.e-date { color: var(--color-on-surface-variant); font-size: 14px; }
</style>
